These fixtures derive from original client and upstream request/response bodies
captured during isolated Copilot validation on 2026-10-09. Each fixture directory
contains the four corresponding bodies. Model names, JSON field structure, tool
contracts, and stream event order retain the observed protocol shape.

Private identifiers, timestamps, opaque replay values, signatures, and environment
details use synthetic placeholders. Authentication exchanges and headers are
excluded. Original diagnostics remain private and are not committed.

CPA's formatted upstream SSE log inserts separators at transport chunk boundaries.
The fixture extraction reassembled split JSON framing. One lost space in
response.instructions was restored from the paired client terminal response.
These upstream fixtures preserve the reconstructed event data, not byte-for-byte
transport framing. Original private logs remain unchanged.

The captured Codex hosted search rotates its opaque identifier between phases and
again in the completed snapshot. Regression expectations retain the completed
snapshot and normalize earlier search lifecycle identifiers to its native ID.
The Claude hosted search fixture retains the provider's unsupported_value error.

The incomplete Responses exchange retains all five native events, reasoning-only
output, provider accounting, usage, and max_output_tokens termination. Response
and reasoning identifiers and encrypted values are distinct across its three
observed phases; stable placeholders preserve that equality pattern. Its upstream
log required chunk reassembly and appended a context-canceled transport diagnostic
after the terminal. That diagnostic is separate from the SSE response body.
